<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51008" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vĭo</span></b> , āre, v. n.
		via, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to go</i>, <i>travel</i> (postAug. and very
			rare; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vio pro eo infelicius fictum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 8, 6, 33</span></i>
			): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">legati intenti ad viandum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 20, 9, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">iter viandi multifidum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prud. adv. Symm. 2, 772</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vians maritus,</span>”
				<i>travelling about</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 10, p. 240</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">6</span></i>, p. 184; <i><span class="en">Flor. 1 <i>init.</i></span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Sol. 29 <i>fin.</i></span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vulg. 1 Reg. 24,
				4</span></i>.—P. a. as <i>subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vĭantes</span></b> , ium, m., <i>travellers</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">viantibus opportunae viae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 15, 10, 2</span></i>
			.</div>
